-independent float64 output class. No inherited infinity discrepancy is accepted.
-The paired launch retains every table plant and checks both members' separate-launch bytes and every
-float64 output class, without an inherited exception.
+HIP's `affine_dot2_stream` keeps its finite-input arithmetic. A non-finite result with an actual non-finite
+input or group-table value is recomputed by the full-group factored float64 formula before its output epilogue.
+Its plain and relu^2 forms check every float64 output class, with no known finding or inherited exception.
+The relu^2 forms also require the separate launches' bytes on every original non-finite plant.
 
